exports[`describeOverview() > a file:  each thing it declares, a type's members grouped 1`] = `
"Card.spell
  type Card  is a Drawable
    The card says what its suits, ranks and colors are:  a deck, a pile or a game only reads them.
    Properties  suit, rank, color, value, direction, name, short suit, short rank, short direction,
                short name, state, picture column, picture, pile
    Actions     is a (suit), is a (rank), is the (rank) of (suits), is a face card,
                is the (color as a color) joker, is face up, is face down, draw it, turn it face up,
                turn it face down, turn it over, play a card
    Constants   Suits (clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades), Ranks (ace, jack, queen, king),
                Colors (red, black), Directions (up, down)
  type Suit
    Properties  color, symbol
  type Rank
    Actions     is a face card
  type Color
  type Joker  is a Card
    A joker:  a wild card with no rank or suit -- there's a red one and a black one
    Properties  color, name, short name, state, picture
  function test card setup
  function test jokers"
`;

exports[`describeThing() > a property, with its compiled javascript 1`] = `
"property color of Card
Card.spell:25

Spell
    - its "color" is the color of its suit

Compiled
  Object.defineProperty(Card.prototype, "color", {
    get() {
      return Suit.color(this.suit)
    },
    configurable: true
  })"
`;

exports[`describeThing() > a type 1`] = `
"type Card is a Drawable
Card.spell:4

The card says what its suits, ranks and colors are:  a deck, a pile or a game only reads them.
A drawable thing:  each card is its own element on the page, e.g. <solitaire-card>.

Properties  suit, rank, color, value, direction, name, short suit, short rank, short direction,
            short name, state, picture column, picture, pile
Actions     is a (suit), is a (rank), is the (rank) of (suits), is a face card,
            is the (color as a color) joker, is face up, is face down, draw it, turn it face up,
            turn it face down, turn it over, play a card
Constants   Suits (clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades), Ranks (ace, jack, queen, king),
            Colors (red, black), Directions (up, down)

Spell
  a "card" is a drawable thing where:
  
    ## suits, ranks and colors:  the card's own kinds of values
    - "suits" as one of clubs, diamonds, hearts or spades
    - "ranks" as one of ace, 2 ... 10, jack, queen or king
    - "colors" as one of red or black
  
    - the "color" of a suit is:
      red if it is diamonds or hearts
      black otherwise
    - the "symbol" of a suit is:
      "♣️" if it is clubs
      "♦️" if it is diamonds
      "♥️" if it is hearts
      "♠️" if it is spades
      "?" otherwise
    - a rank "is a face card" if it is jack, queen or king
  
    ## its suit and rank
    - its "suit" is a suit
    - its "rank" is a rank
    - its "color" is the color of its suit
    - its "value" is the position of its rank      // ace 1 ... king 13
  
    - it "is a (suit)"                              // e.g. "the card is a spade"
    - it "is a (rank)"                              // e.g. "the card is a queen"
    - it "is the (rank) of (suits)"                 // e.g. "the card is the queen of spades"
    - it "is a face card" if its rank is a face card
    - it "is the (color as a color) joker" if it is a joker and its color is color
  
    ## its direction:  face up or face down
    - its "direction" is up or down
    - it "is face up" if its direction is up
    - it "is face down" if its direction is down
  
    ## its names
    - its "name" is: its rank + "-of-" + its suit   // e.g. "queen-of-spades"
    - its "short suit" is the symbol of its suit
    - its "short rank" is:
      "?" if its rank is nothing
      "" + its rank if its rank is a number
      the first character of its rank as uppercase otherwise
    - its "short direction" is:
      "+" if its direction is up
      "—" otherwise
    - its "short name" is: its short rank + its short suit
    - its "state" is: its short rank + its short suit + its short direction
  
    ## its picture:  a character of unicode's Playing Cards
    // SEE:  https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/block/U+1F0A0
    // The block is a grid:  a row for each suit, and in each row, a column for each rank.
    // - The rows start at 1F0A0 (spades), 1F0B0 (hearts), 1F0C0 (diamonds) and 1F0D0 (clubs).
    // - The columns run ace 1, 2 ... 10, jack B, then a knight our deck doesn't have, C, then queen D and king E.
    - its "picture column" is:
      its value + 1 if it is a queen or it is a king      // past the knight
      its value otherwise
    - its "picture" is:
      unicode 1F0A0 + its picture column if it is a spade
      unicode 1F0B0 + its picture column if it is a heart
      unicode 1F0C0 + its picture column if it is a diamond
      unicode 1F0D0 + its picture column otherwise
  
    ## drawing:  its picture face up, the back every card shares face down
    - to draw it:
      if it is face down
        return <ui-text class="Card" size="massive" color="blue" onClick={fire event card click with card = it}>
          {unicode 1F0A0}
        </ui-text>
      return <ui-text class="Card" size="massive" color={its color} onClick={fire event card click with card = it}>
        {its picture}
      </ui-text>
  
    ## turning it over
    // each pauses a moment, so \`wait for: turn the card face up\` animates
    - to turn it face up:
      set its direction to up
      pause for 50 msec
    - to turn it face down:
      set its direction to down
      pause for 50 msec
    - to turn it over:
      if it is face up: turn it face down
      otherwise: turn it face up
      pause for 50 msec"
`;
